       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order, even with your confirmation. Acetaminophen 3,000 mg three times daily is 9,000 mg/day. That dose carries a high risk of acute liver injury or liver failure, and I can't think of a clinical situation where it would be appropriate. Normal liver function and a weight of 70 kg don't change that. You also haven't given a rationale, and a single 3,000 mg dose is about three times the usual maximum.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n- **Enter a safe dose right away.** For example, 1,000 mg PO three times daily (3,000 mg/day), or 1,000 mg PO every 6 hours (4,000 mg/day maximum).\n- **Help with a different goal.** If you're trying to get more analgesia, I can enter an adjunct such as an NSAID, if appropriate, or other options you choose.\n- **Check for a typo.** If you meant 3,000 mg/day total, I can enter 1,000 mg three times daily.\n\nIf you believe there's a rare indication for this dose, please talk to pharmacy or clinical toxicology. Any order outside standard limits should go through their review and not be entered by me."
